# Region geometry

A-within (median across configurations): **0.001342**

## Does A-within track batch_size?

batch_size is the only tunable that changes how much training happens (`num_steps = budget / batch_size`), so it is the suspect for why noise varies inside a region. Architecture is frozen here, which is what makes this separable at all.

| configuration | batch_size | seeds | std |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| r0.05_c1 | 19852.0 | 3 | 0.001117 |
| r0.02_c4 | 21160.0 | 3 | 0.001007 |
| r0.02_c1 | 22136.0 | 3 | 0.001342 |
| r0.05_c4 | 22576.0 | 3 | 0.000951 |
| r0.02_c2 | 23243.0 | 3 | 0.002304 |
| r0.05_c0 | 26083.0 | 3 | 0.001797 |
| r0.10_c0 | 29373.0 | 3 | 0.001685 |

## B(r): is there anything left to find inside a fence of radius r?

`real signal = sqrt(B_observed^2 - A_within^2)` -- the observed spread already contains the noise. A region is saturated when real signal falls to A-within.

| radius | configs | B observed | real signal | real / A-within |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 0.02 | 5 | 0.001345 | 0.000095 | 0.07 |
| 0.05 | 5 | 0.010800 | 0.010716 | 7.99 |

## Recommended fence radius

**0.05** -- the smallest tested radius whose real signal is at least 3x A-within.


